---
import Layout from '/src/layouts/Layout.astro'
import TechStackBadges from '/src/components/TechStackBadges.astro'
import { t } from '/src/i18n/utils'
import { primaryStack, toolingStack } from '/src/data/techStack'

const i = t('en')
---

<Layout title={i.about.title} description={i.about.description} pageType="about">
  <section class="about">
    <h1>{i.about.heading}</h1>
    <p>
      I'm a software developer with over a decade of experience, focused on
      frontend and comfortable across the full stack. I build frontend-heavy
      products and the tools around them: Vue/Nuxt and React/Next applications,
      TypeScript-heavy interfaces, the Node.js/GraphQL services behind them,
      small CLI utilities, editor integrations, and self-hosted systems that
      solve real day-to-day problems. I also care a lot about a fast,
      keyboard-driven workflow.
    </p>

    <h2>What I Do</h2>
    <p>
      I specialize in Vue and Nuxt with TypeScript, and I'm equally at home in
      React and Next.js. A lot of the work is bringing existing codebases
      forward — migrating legacy UIs to modern stacks and typing JavaScript
      projects end to end — without stopping delivery. I've owned frontend
      architecture at scale: feature-sliced design, micro-frontends with Module
      Federation, backend-for-frontend layers, and shared UI kits documented in
      Storybook.
    </p>
    <p>
      I work across the stack when a project calls for it: building and
      integrating backends in Node.js and TypeScript, designing GraphQL and REST
      APIs (with some PHP along the way), and shipping a few AI integrations —
      from AI-assisted content features to streaming model output straight into
      the interface.
    </p>
    <p>
      I've led frontend work on production applications across media, fintech,
      telecom, and security: high-traffic sites, real-time collaborative
      editors, live dashboards, and streaming-data interfaces — usually in
      English-speaking international teams. Alongside the UI I set up the
      infrastructure that keeps a project healthy: CI/CD pipelines, unit and
      end-to-end tests, and quality gates. I care about maintainable code that
      other developers can work with — boring abstractions where possible, tests
      where behavior matters, and documentation that explains the decisions
      rather than repeating the code.
    </p>

    <section class="tech-section" aria-labelledby="tech-stack-title">
      <h2 id="tech-stack-title">Tech Stack</h2>
      <div class="stack-groups">
        <div>
          <h3>Frontend</h3>
          <TechStackBadges items={primaryStack} ariaLabel="Frontend stack" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Tools</h3>
          <TechStackBadges items={toolingStack} ariaLabel="Tooling stack" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <h2>Open Source and Writing</h2>
    <p>
      I also build small open-source tools when an annoyance keeps repeating:
      Telegram media bots, terminal helpers, editor plugins, and experiments
      around self-hosting. A lot of that comes from a habit of optimizing how I
      work: a keyboard-driven, mostly mouseless setup on a tiling window manager
      (i3), keybindings grouped into muscle memory, and lightweight tools that
      keep the machine responsive. The blog is where I write down the practical parts:
      what broke, what fixed it, and what I would do differently next time. You
      can find the code on <a href="https://github.com/antlis">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: 640px;
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  .about h1 {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .tech-section {
    margin: 2.8rem 0 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .tech-section h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 1.35rem;
  }

  .stack-groups {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.85rem;
  }

  .stack-groups > div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .stack-groups h3 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    line-height: 1.25;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .stack-groups > div + div {
    padding-top: 0.1rem;
  }

  .about p {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.95rem + 0.25vw, 1.1rem);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .about a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .about a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-hover);
  }
</style>
